              "description": "executePutCountersIndependentMultiTarget implements the",
              "doc": "executePutCountersIndependentMultiTarget implements the\nput_counters_independent_multi_target primitive (ticket\nengine.auto-put-counters-independent-multi-target-8814b1cc89, River\nHeralds' Boon class): \"Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature and a\n+1/+1 counter on up to one target Merfolk.\" TWO independently resolved\ntargets in one non-modal spell resolution \u2014 targets[0] is the MANDATORY\nslot (filters[0]), targets[1] is the OPTIONAL \"up to one\" slot\n(filters[1]): an absent/declined second target is simply skipped rather\nthan an error, mirroring executeDestroyUpToArtifactCreatureLand's\noptional-slot tolerance, while validating each positional target\nagainst its OWN filter (not one shared filter) mirrors\nexecuteDestroyMultiFilterTargets. Distinct from the \"each\" mass-shape\n(a counter on EVERY qualifying permanent) and the modal round-2 shape\n(player picks one of several modes) handled by executePutCounterEffect\nabove \u2014 this always resolves BOTH slots of one fixed, non-modal effect.\n",
              "end": 14302,
